            <ArticleTitle>[A man with dyspnoea after a kidney transplant].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D1782</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a 62-year-old man with a kidney transplant in the past. Because of progressive dyspnoea a CT-scan was made, which showed ground glass in the upper fields with calcifications. He was diagnosed with metastatic pulmonary calcification, which is mostly seen in patient with renal failure and secondary hyperparathyroidism.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
